PrimerMapper 3.2
================

PrimerMapper is a Perl/Tkx GUI for PCR primer design, SNP-flanking primer
design, allele-specific primer generation, primer visualization, and remote
NCBI sequence retrieval.

INSTALLATION

From this directory:

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

DEPENDENCIES

External program:

  primer3_core

Required Perl modules:

  Tkx
  LWP::Simple
  LWP::UserAgent
  Bio::SeqIO
  Bio::Graphics
  Bio::SeqFeature::Generic

RUNNING

From the top-level PrimerMapper-fixed directory:

   perl PrimerMapper_driver.pl

On macOS with the dependency-fixed Homebrew Perl/local-lib setup:

   conda deactivate 2>/dev/null || true
   export PM_PERL="$HOME/perl5-primermapper"
   export BREW_PERL="$(brew --prefix perl)/bin/perl"
   eval "$("$BREW_PERL" -I"$PM_PERL/lib/perl5" -Mlocal::lib="$PM_PERL")"
   cd ~/Desktop/PrimerMapper-fixed
   "$BREW_PERL" PrimerMapper_driver.pl

INPUT NOTES

Regular primer design requires FASTA input beginning with a descriptor line:

   >example_sequence
   ATGCGTACGTACGTACGTACGTACGTACGTAC

SNP primer design requires a FASTA header containing pos=N.len, and the base
at that coordinate must be an IUPAC ambiguity code:

   >example_snp pos=25.len=80
   ATGCGTACGTACGTACGTACGTACRACGTACGTACGTACGTACGTACGTAC

ERROR-CHECKING CHANGES IN 3.2

PrimerMapper now shows GUI messages rather than stack traces for common input
and design problems, including invalid product-size ranges, invalid primer
settings, missing FASTA descriptor lines, missing SNP coordinates, SNP
coordinates outside the sequence, missing IUPAC SNP bases, and primer3 runs
that return no primer pairs.

